{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ROM",
  "chapter": 14,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Him that is weak in the faith receive ye, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not to doubtful disputations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For one believeth that he may eat all things: another, who is weak, eateth herbs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not him that eateth, despise him that eateth not; and let not him who eateth not, judge him that eateth: for God hath received him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who art thou that judgest another man's servant? to his own master he standeth or falleth: and he shall be held up: for God is able to make him stand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One man esteemeth one day above another: another esteemeth every day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "alike",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Let every man be fully persuaded in his own mind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that regardeth the day, regardeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the Lord: and he that regardeth not the day, to the Lord he doth not regard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". He that eateth, eateth to the Lord, for he giveth God thanks; and he that eateth not, to the Lord he eateth not, and giveth God thanks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For none of us liveth to himself, and no man dieth to himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For whether we live, we live to the Lord; and whether we die, we die to the Lord: whether we live therefore, or die, we are the Lord's.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For to this end Christ both died, and rose, and revived, that he might be Lord both of the dead and the living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But why dost thou judge thy brother? or why dost thou set at naught thy brother? for we shall all stand before the judgment-seat of Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is written, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I live, saith the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So then every one of us shall give account of himself to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us not therefore judge one another any more: but judge this rather, that no man put a stumbling-block, or an occasion to fall in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brother's way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know, and am persuaded by the Lord Jesus, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing unclean by itself: but to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unclean.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if thy brother is grieved with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " food, now walkest thou not charitably. Destroy not him with thy food, for whom Christ died.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not then your good be evil spoken of:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the kingdom of God is not food and drink, but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he that in these things serveth Christ, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " acceptable to God, and approved by men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us therefore follow after the things which make for peace, and things with which one may edify another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the sake of food, destroy not the work of God. All things indeed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " evil for that man who eateth with offense.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good neither to eat flesh, nor to drink wine, nor ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by which thy brother stumbleth, or is offended, or is made weak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou faith? have it to thyself before God. Happy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that condemneth not himself in that thing which he alloweth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.14.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.14.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he that doubteth is damned if he eateth, because ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he eateth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not from faith: for whatever ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not from faith is sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
